// The core of the bundled library: the functions and members every file uses without an
// import. It is a prelude module, so a file's own declaration or import of a name shadows it.
// Every declaration here is an intrinsic: the compiler types and lowers its calls itself.
package prism

// Writes the text form of `value` to the standard output: an `Int` in decimal, a `Double`, a
// `Bool` as `true` or `false`, a `Char`, a `String` as its text, and any other value as the
// text its `toString()` returns. It takes any argument a string template part takes.
public intrinsic fun <T> print(value: &T): Unit

// Writes the text form of `value`, as `print` does, then a newline. Without an argument it
// writes the newline alone.
public intrinsic fun <T> println(value: &T): Unit

// The decimal text of this `Int`, with a leading `-` when it is negative.
public intrinsic fun Int.toString(): String

// The text of this `Double`, as `print` writes it.
public intrinsic fun Double.toString(): String

// `true` or `false`.
public intrinsic fun Bool.toString(): String

// The one-character text of this `Char`.
public intrinsic fun Char.toString(): String

// The number of characters of this `String`.
public intrinsic val String.length: Int
